Lucid Engine libass patch series: upstream libass pull request, unchanged.

Origin: libass/libass pull request #951 ("render: cache rendered events")
by Kacper Michajłow (kasper93), at its head commit
f96a521a03ef74d97e74876b800c22b67c9b89a5, the pull request's only commit.
The pull request was open, not merged, when this was fetched.
Source: https://github.com/libass/libass/commit/f96a521a03ef74d97e74876b800c22b67c9b89a5.patch
Pull request: https://github.com/libass/libass/pull/951
Fetched from libass's own repository by that commit hash on 14 October
2026. Everything from the "From f96a521a..." line down is the published
patch, byte for byte, including its author attribution. It applies to
libass 0.17.5 after patch 0001 without fuzz or offsets; nothing needed
changing. Static events (no \move, \fad, \t, karaoke or scrolling
effect) are rendered once and their images reused while nothing they
depend on changes, so an unchanged sign with a vector clip or a line with
a background box is no longer reported as changed on every frame. Vivid's
patch 0010 closes the gaps it leaves. libass is licensed ISC, and so is
this patch.

From f96a521a03ef74d97e74876b800c22b67c9b89a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Kacper=20Michaj=C5=82ow?= <kasper93@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:57:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] render: cache rendered events

Cache the finished image list of time-invariant events, keyed by the
event text, style, margins and a state generation id. The generation
identifies an exact snapshot of all renderer settings and track state
the output depends on, compared by memcmp at the start of every frame,
so all key components compare exactly. Entries are evicted LRU at a 32
MiB budget.

Re-rendering an unchanged event with 512 KiB of text: 161 -> 0.1 ms.
